# Public discovery shell

The public primary navigation uses clear product destinations: **Brand Kit** (`/create/brand-kit`), **Create** (`/create`), **Utilities** (`/utilities`), **Learn** (`/learn`), and **Platform** (`/platform`). The UnionOps wordmark links Home. Brand Kit is a direct, always-visible setup destination — not a Create catalog peer. Guided setup lives at `/start` (Home CTA + footer), not in primary nav. At narrow widths expose the labeled Menu control, whose first-level drawer repeats the same destinations. Search (`/search`) is a separate utility action. Keep language, display, and account controls separate from primary navigation. Session/env-gated Officer Hub and Local Portal links remain operational shortcuts when applicable; Platform explains the hosted products to logged-out visitors.

Use direct, descriptive links rather than public mega-menus, circular launch cards, or icon-only navigation. Keep desktop and mobile labels aligned. Mobile navigation must retain visible focus, Escape-to-close, focus return, and a keyboard trap while open. The authenticated Hub and Portal keep their own navigation.

## One public catalog

`src/lib/comms/public-catalog.ts` is the discovery registry for tools, guides, steward playbooks, Officer Learning modules, workshops, and reference libraries. Derive Create, Utilities, Learn, Search, breadcrumbs, related links, and sitemap coverage from it. Tools carry `toolSurface: "create" | "utilities"`. Keep legacy content registries only as source data where they still power existing pages. Preserve feature gates, signed-in visibility, and platform/tenant-disabled tool filtering.

Catalog copy lives in `messages/en.json` and `messages/fr.json`; do not fork public content into Markdown trees. Search and filters run in the browser over localized registry content, with query/filter state reflected in the URL. Do not add analytics or third-party search. Every card states a useful outcome, audience, approximate time, concrete deliverable, and whether work/progress stays in this browser, can optionally be copied to Officer Hub, uses Officer Hub, or is reading-only. A broad format label is not a substitute for the deliverable. Estimates remain approximate and need content-owner review.

## Home and guided setup

Home explains Brand Kit as the foundation, then **parallel** destinations Create / Utilities / Learn, then Platform as the hosted layer for shared local operations. Do **not** present a numbered five-step sequence that implies users must visit every area in order. Link to `/start` as **Guided setup** for role checklists. Brand Kit completion is inferred from local browser state; never imply it is a union-wide shared profile.

Learn starts with curated task collections (including **Comms getting started** at `/learn/first-week`). Continue to test whether the flat catalog needs more progressive grouping with real visitors before adding more categories or search infrastructure.

Home has one value proposition, Brand Kit as primary setup, a product preview, parallel toolkit destinations, a Platform band, and secondary guided setup. Keep exhaustive channel lists and workshop facilitation details in Learn, not on Home. Do not dump the full tool inventory on Home.

## Canonical routes

| Retired path | Canonical path |
|---|---|
| `/onboarding` | `/start?step=brand` |
| `/brand-kit` | `/create/brand-kit` |
| `/tools` | `/create` |
| `/tools/:creative-slug` | `/create/:slug` |
| `/tools/:utility-slug` and `/create/:utility-slug` | `/utilities/:slug` |
| `/guides` | `/learn` |
| `/guide` | `/learn/communications-blueprint` |
| `/guide/social-media-plan` | `/learn/first-week` |
| `/guide/steward-playbooks` | `/learn/steward` |
| `/guide/officer-learning/:slug` | `/learn/officer/:slug` |
| `/guide/workshops/:slug` | `/learn/workshops/:slug` |
| `/examples`, `/captions`, `/assets` | `/learn/library/:slug` |
| Other `/guide/:slug` | `/learn/:slug` |

Utility slug list: `UTILITY_TOOL_SLUGS` in `src/lib/seo/utility-tool-slugs.ts` (re-exported from `nav-config.ts`). Keep locale-aware permanent redirects in `PUBLIC_ROUTE_REDIRECTS`, and keep internal `Link` targets, canonical/hreflang metadata, and sitemap paths on the new routes. Query strings and fragments must survive route migration. Do not remove redirects; bookmarks and search equity are part of the product.

Privacy and security copy must distinguish Comms that stays on-device from hosted Officer Hub / Local Portal data. Do not imply Hub storage is local-only or promise that the whole platform is free forever.

## Footer

Keep the footer compact for secondary/trust links: Home, Guided setup, What's New, About UnionOps, Privacy, Security, Accessibility, Support, Feedback, and Install. Do **not** repeat Brand Kit, Create, Utilities, Learn, or Platform there — those belong in primary navigation.

## Living decision log

Product IA decisions for this shell live in [`docs/UX_PRODUCT_REFACTOR.md`](../../docs/UX_PRODUCT_REFACTOR.md). Brand Kit is the foundation; Create, Utilities, and Learn are parallel on-device destinations; Platform is the hosted operational layer — not a fifth forced Home step.
